cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the relevant methodological references listed in the documentation."
type: software
title: "blrfit: broad AGN emission lines against the narrow-line systemic velocity"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ektrnddn/blrfit"
authors:
  - family-names: Dadiani
    given-names: Ekaterine
    affiliation: "Carnegie Mellon University"
    email: edadiani@andrew.cmu.edu
keywords:
  - active galactic nuclei
  - broad emission lines
  - spectroscopy
  - supermassive black hole binaries
  - DESI
  - SDSS
abstract: >-
  Fits the broad Halpha and Hbeta emission-line profiles of a single AGN spectrum,
  measures offsets relative to the fitted narrow-line reference, and reports
  profile classes, quality flags and optional conditional Monte Carlo errors.
  Accepts public DESI identifiers or coordinates, local DESI and SDSS files, and
  explicitly mapped spectral tables or images with wavelength, flux, statistical
  noise and redshift. Version 0.2.0 preserves the RC1 numerical fitter. Its fixed
  synthetic uncertainty study passed 67 criteria and left five inconclusive;
  universal survey-error calibration is not established. Mg II and between-epoch
  velocity routines remain experimental.
